<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>9.4.4: Three Different Methods for Solving an Equation</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02394</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.4.4: Three Different Methods for Solving an Equation</md:title>
    <md:uuid>b13fc9cb-15e5-4c59-805a-3c5f0307c121</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<para>Here are three methods for solving \(3x^2+8x+5=0\).</para>
<para>Carefully examine each method.</para>
<table class="os-raise-wideequaltable">
  <tgroup cols="3"><tbody><row>
      <entry><emphasis>Method 1:</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>Method 2:</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>Method 3:</emphasis></entry></row>
  <row>
      <entry><para>\(\begin{array}{rcl} 3 x^{2}+8 x+5 &amp;=&amp;0 \\ (3 x+5)(x+1) &amp;=&amp;0 \\ x+1 &amp;=&amp;0 \\ 3 x+5
        &amp;=&amp;0 \\ x &amp;=&amp;-1 \\ 3 x &amp;=&amp;-5 \\ x &amp;=&amp;-\frac{5}{3} \end{array}\) </para>
        <para>\(x=-\frac{5}{3} \text { and } x=-1\)</para></entry>
      <entry><para>\(\begin{aligned} 3 x^{2}+8 x+5 &amp;=0 \\ 9 x^{2}+24 x+15 &amp;=0 \\ (3 x)^{2}+8(3 x)+15 &amp;=0 \\ U^{2}+8 U+15
        &amp;=0 \\ (U+5)(U+3) &amp;=0 \\ U+5 &amp;=0 \\ U+3 &amp;=0 \\ U &amp;=-5 \\ U &amp;=-3 \\ 3 x &amp;=-5 \\ 3 x
        &amp;=-3 \end{aligned} \) </para>
        <para>\(x=-\frac{5}{3} \text { and } x=-1\)</para></entry>
      <entry><para>\(\begin{aligned} 3 x^{2}+8 x+5 &amp;=0 \\ 9 x^{2}+24 x+15 &amp;=0 \\ 9 x^{2}+24 x+16 &amp;=1 \\ (3 x+4)^{2} &amp;=1
        \\ 3 x+4 &amp;=1 \\ 3 x+4 &amp;=-1\end{aligned}\) </para>
        <para>\(x=-\frac{5}{3} \text { and } x=-1\)</para></entry>
    </row>
  </tbody></tgroup></table>

<para>Once you understand the methods, use each method at least one time to solve these equations.</para>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>\(5x^2+17x+6=0\)</para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  
  <para>Method 1 is used here, but any of the three methods would work.</para>
  
  <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl} 5 x^2+17 x+6 &amp;=&amp; 0 \\ (5x+2)(x+3) &amp;=&amp; 0 \\ 5x+2 &amp;=&amp; 0 \\ 5x &amp;=&amp; -2 \\ x&amp;=&amp; - \frac{2}{5} \\ x+3 &amp;=&amp; 0 \\ x &amp;=&amp; -3 \end{array} \)</para>
  
  <para>\(x=-\frac{2}{5} \text { and } x =-3\)</para>

</solution></exercise>
</example>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>\(6x^2+19x=-10\)</para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  
  <para>Method 2 is used here, but any of the three methods would work.</para>
  
  <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}6x^2+19x&amp;=&amp;-10\\6x^2+19x+10&amp;=&amp;0 \\ 36x^2+114x+60&amp;=&amp;0 \\ (6x)^2+19(6x)+60&amp;=&amp;0 \\ U^2+19U+60&amp;=&amp;0 \\ (U+15)(U+4)&amp;=&amp;0 \\ U+15&amp;=&amp;0 \\ U&amp;=&amp;-15\\6x&amp;=&amp;-15 \\ x&amp;=&amp;-\frac{15}6=-\frac52 \\ (U+4)&amp;=&amp;0 \\ U&amp;=&amp;-4 \\ 6x&amp;=&amp;-4 \\ x&amp;=&amp;-\frac46=-\frac23\end{array}\)</para>
  
  <para>\(x=-\frac{5}{2} \text { and } x=-\frac{2}{3}\)</para>

</solution></exercise>
</example>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>\(8x^2−33x+4=0\)</para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  
  <para>Method 1 is used here, but any of the three methods would work.</para>
  
  <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl} 8 x^{2}-33 x+4 &amp;=&amp;0 \\ (8 x-1)(x-4) &amp;=&amp;0 \\ 8 x-1 &amp;=&amp;0 \\ 8 x &amp;=&amp;1 \\ x &amp;=&amp;\frac{1}{8} \\ x-4 &amp;=0 \\ x &amp;=&amp;4 \end{array} \) </para>
  
  <para>\(x=\frac{1}{8} \text { and } x=4\)</para>

</solution></exercise>
</example>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>\(8x^2−26x=-21\)</para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  
  <para>Method 1 is used here, but any of the three methods would work.</para>
  
  <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl} 8 x^{2}-26 x &amp;=&amp;-21 \\ 8 x^{2}-26 x+21 &amp;=&amp;0 \\ (4 x-7)(2 x-3) &amp;=&amp;0 \\ 4 x-7 &amp;=&amp;0 \\ 4 x &amp;=&amp;7 \\ x &amp;=&amp;\frac{7}{4} \\ 2 x-3 &amp;=&amp;0 \\ 2 x &amp;=&amp;3 \\ x &amp;=&amp;\frac{3}{2} \\ x=\frac{7}{4} \text { and } x=\frac{3}{2} \end{array} \) </para>

</solution></exercise>
</example><example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>\(10x^2+37x=36\)</para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  
  <para>Method 3 is used here, but any of the three methods would work.</para>
  
  <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl} 10x^{2}+37x &amp;=&amp;36 \\ \frac{(10x^{2}+37x)}{10} &amp;=&amp;\frac{36}{10} \\ x^{2}+\frac{37}{10}x &amp;=&amp;\frac{36}{10} \\ x^2+\frac{37}{10}x+((\frac{1}{2})(\frac{37}{10}))^{2} &amp;=&amp;\frac{36}{10}+((\frac{1}{2})(\frac{37}{10}))^{2} \\ x^2+\frac{37}{10}x+\frac{1369}{400} &amp;=&amp;\frac{36}{10}+\frac{1369}{400} \\ x^2+\frac{37}{10}x+\frac{1369}{400} &amp;=&amp;\frac{2809}{400} \\ (x+\frac{37}{20})^{2} &amp;=&amp;\frac{2809}{400} \\ \sqrt{(x+\frac{37}{20})^{2}} &amp;=&amp;\sqrt{\frac{2809}{400}}\\ x+\frac{37}{20} &amp;=&amp;\frac{53}{20} \\ x &amp;=&amp;\frac{16}{20} \\ x &amp;=&amp;\frac{4}{5} \\ x+\frac{37}{20} &amp;=&amp;-\frac{53}{20} \\ x &amp;=&amp;-\frac{90}{20} \\ x &amp;=&amp;-\frac{9}{2} \end{array} \)</para>
  
  <para>\(x=\frac{4}{5} \text { and } x=-\frac{9}{2}\)</para>

</solution></exercise>
</example><example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>\(12x^2+20x−77=0\)</para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  
  <para>Method 3 is used here, but any of the three methods would work.</para>
  
  <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}12x^2+20x-77&amp;=&amp;0\\12x^2+20x&amp;=&amp;77\\\frac{\left(12x^2+20x\right)}{12}&amp;=&amp;\frac{77}{12}\\x^2+\frac{20}{12}x&amp;=&amp;\frac{77}{12}\\x^2+\frac{20}{12}x+\left(\left(\frac12\right)\left(\frac{20}{12}\right)\right)^2&amp;=&amp;\frac{77}{12}+\left(\left(\frac12\right)\left(\frac{20}{12}\right)\right)^2\\x^2+\frac{20}{12}x+\frac{100}{144}&amp;=&amp;\frac{77}{12}+\frac{100}{144}=\frac{924}{144}+\frac{100}{144}\\x^2+\frac{20}{12}x+\frac{100}{144}&amp;=&amp;\frac{1024}{144}\\\left(x+\frac{10}{12}\right)^2&amp;=&amp;\frac{1024}{144}\\\sqrt{\left(x+\frac{10}{12}\right)^2}&amp;=&amp;\sqrt{\frac{1024}{144}}\\x+\frac{10}{12}&amp;=&amp;\frac{32}{12}\\x+\frac{10}{12}&amp;=&amp;-\frac{32}{12}\\x&amp;=&amp;\frac{22}{12}\\x&amp;=&amp;-\frac{42}{12}\\x&amp;=&amp;\frac{11}6\\x&amp;=&amp;-\frac{21}6=-\frac72\end{array}\) </para>
  
  <para>\(x=\frac{11}6\text{ and }x=-\frac72\)</para>

</solution></exercise>
</example>
